	"item": [
		{
			"name": "8. Sign-up and email (010b)",
			"description": "Sign-up and email confirmation (010b, 23/11). Runs only with env runSignupTests = true: it creates a real account and sends real emails (plus-addressed from test_account_email, e.g. you+010b-main-<time>@...). Never sets bearerToken; the new account's token is bearerToken_signup.\n\nOrder: run 8A and 8B (8B-3 waits 61 s). Then copy the token from email 2's link (or the users row) into env signupVerifyToken (and, optionally, email 1's token into signupVerifyTokenOld) and run 8C. 8C-2 clears both after use.\n\nNeeds: Xano X1–X5 from Project/Plan/010b-xano-prompts.md, with terms_accepted and terms_version optional inputs (so 8A-3 gets TERMS_REQUIRED).",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "8A · Sign-up",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "8A-1 · POST /auth/signup — new account (terms accepted)",
							"event": [
								{
									"listen": "prerequest",
									"script": {
										"type": "text/javascript",
										"exec": [
											"if (String(pm.environment.get(\"runSignupTests\")) !== \"true\") { console.log(\"Skipped: set env runSignupTests = true (creates a real account and sends emails)\"); pm.execution.skipRequest(); }",
											"const base = String(pm.environment.get(\"test_account_email\") || \"\");",
											"const at = base.indexOf(\"@\");",
											"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"signupEmail\", base.slice(0, at) + \"+010b-main-\" + Date.now() + base.slice(at));",
											"[\"bearerToken_signup\",\"signupUserId\",\"signupSessionId\"].forEach(k => pm.collectionVariables.unset(k));"
										]
									}
								},
								{
									"listen": "test",
									"script": {
										"type": "text/javascript",
										"exec": [
											"const j = () => { try { return pm.response.json() || {}; } catch (e) { return {}; } };",
											"const code = () => ((j().payload || {}).code);",
											"pm.test(\"8A-1: 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
											"pm.test(\"8A-1: userid, authToken, refreshToken, session_id\", () => { const b = j(); pm.expect(b.userid).to.be.a(\"number\"); pm.expect(b.authToken).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty; pm.expect(b.refreshToken).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty; pm.expect(b.session_id).to.exist; });",
											"if (j().authToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"bearerToken_signup\", j().authToken); pm.collectionVariables.set(\"signupUserId\", j().userid); pm.collectionVariables.set(\"signupSessionId\", j().session_id); }",
											"console.log(\"8A-1 new account:\", pm.collectionVariables.get(\"signupEmail\"), \"id\", j().userid, \"- check the users row: terms_accepted_at, terms_version, email_verification_token, email_ver_expires_at; email 1 should arrive\");"
										]
									}
								}
							],
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json"
									}
